  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In July 2025 testimony, Jonathan Morrison said properly developed and operated automated vehicles could prevent the vast majority of crashes, injuries, and fatalities caused by human choices and errors. He also said technologies such as automated vehicles offer potential safety and efficiency benefits but are complex and introduce application-specific risks. Morrison called for NHTSA leadership and a safety framework of guidance and regulation for automated vehicles, and said realizing their benefits depends on consumer trust rooted in safety.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "In July 2025 testimony, Jonathan Morrison said properly developed and operated automated vehicles could prevent the vast majority of crashes, injuries, and fatalities caused by human choices and errors.",
